{"version": 2, "width": 96, "height": 82, "timestamp": 1794479094, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}}
[0.2, "o", "\u001b[1mResearch Agent demo\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.2, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.5, "o", "What it does, in 4 steps:\r\n"]
[2.5, "o", "  1. Searches PubMed for the 5 most relevant papers\r\n"]
[3.5, "o", "  2. Claude summarises them into short claims, each citing its paper\r\n"]
[4.5, "o", "  3. Each claim is checked against its paper (exact quotes + every number)\r\n"]
[5.5, "o", "  4. Saves everything to an audit record (JSON)\r\n"]
[6.5, "o", "\r\n"]
[6.8, "o", "How to read the output:\r\n"]
[7.8, "o", "  \u001b[32m✔\u001b[0m verified claim, with its source (first author, year, journal, link)\r\n"]
[8.8, "o", "  ✘ failed claims are only counted; reasons are in the audit record\r\n"]
[9.8, "o", "\r\n"]
[10.1, "o", "\u001b[2mPersonal project · public PubMed data only · costs about $0.01 per run\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[14.6, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[1mResearch Agent demo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m· search → summarise → check → audit record\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[15.1, "o", "$ python -m research_agent \"metformin type 2 diabetes HbA1c randomized\" --yes\r\n"]
[55.72, "o", "Research Agent · \"metformin type 2 diabetes HbA1c randomized\"\r\n────────────────────────────────────────\r\nPapers 5 · Claims 12 · ✔ Verified 8 · ✘ Failed 4\r\nSkipped 0 · Rejected 0 · Injection warnings 0\r\n────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n✔ 1. In the ATOMIC trial, the proportion of patients with increased HbA1c was 62% in the\r\n     combination group versus 15% in the comparator group, and no previously unknown\r\n     adverse drug events were reported.\r\n     Lee JE et al. 2024 · Diabetes & metabolism journal\r\n     https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38763510/\r\n\r\n✔ 2. The authors concluded that adding atorvastatin to metformin improved HbA1c and\r\n     LDL-C more than either drug alone, and suggested metformin may prevent\r\n     atorvastatin's glucose-raising effect.\r\n     Lee JE et al. 2024 · Diabetes & metabolism journal\r\n     https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38763510/\r\n\r\n✔ 3. Initial treatment failure occurred in 43.6% of the early combination group versus\r\n     62.1% of the metformin monotherapy group during the first study period.\r\n     Matthews DR et al. 2019 · Lancet (London, England)\r\n     https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31542292/\r\n\r\n✔ 4. Both treatment approaches in VERIFY were safe and well tolerated, with no\r\n     unexpected safety findings and no treatment-related deaths.\r\n     Matthews DR et al. 2019 · Lancet (London, England)\r\n     https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31542292/\r\n\r\n✔ 5. In a 12-week trial of patients with type 2 diabetes, add-on empagliflozin reduced\r\n     HbA1c by -1.8% versus -0.69% with metformin add-on arm changes reported, and\r\n     produced greater reductions in weight, systolic and diastolic blood pressure than\r\n     the metformin group.\r\n     Mesri Alamdari N et al. 2025 · BMC research notes\r\n     https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40745313/\r\n\r\n✔ 6. Empagliflozin add-on also reduced fasting blood sugar more than metformin (-23.1 vs\r\n     -15.25 mg/dl) and was associated with lower triglycerides and higher HDL-c compared\r\n     with the metformin group.\r\n     Mesri Alamdari N et al. 2025 · BMC research notes\r\n     https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40745313/\r\n\r\n✔ 7. In a 16-week open-label Phase 3 study in Indian patients with type 2 diabetes,\r\n     triple fixed-dose dapagliflozin, sitagliptin and metformin IR reduced HbA1c by\r\n     -2.08% versus -1.38% with the sitagliptin plus metformin dual combination.\r\n     Singh MP et al. 2025 · Advances in therapy\r\n     https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40828352/\r\n\r\n✔ 8. In the same study, 48.9% of patients on the triple combination reached HbA1c below\r\n     7% versus 31.1% on the dual combination, and both regimens were well tolerated.\r\n     Singh MP et al. 2025 · Advances in therapy\r\n     https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40828352/\r\n\r\n✘ Failed: 4 (reasons in the audit record)\r\n\r\nAudit record: runs/20261112T102459Z_3b55c28e.json\r\n"]
